  {
   "id": "ifc_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 158,
   "width": 964,
   "height": 165,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100006,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700042,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "VariantAssigner   -> HashBucketAssigner\n     assign(experimentId, userId, experimentDef) -> variantKey\nExposureLogger    -> AsyncExposureLogger\n     logExposure(experimentId, userId, variantKey, timestamp)   # fire-and-forget\nMetricAggregator  -> WelfordMetricAggregator\n     ingest(experimentId, variantKey, metricName, value)\nSignificanceTest  -> TwoProportionZTest | WelchTTest\n     evaluate(controlSummary, treatmentSummary) -> {pValue, confidenceInterval}\nSrmChecker        -> ChiSquareSrmChecker\n     check(observedCounts, expectedAllocation) -> {chiSquareStat, pValue, flagged}\nExperimentAnalyzer  - the orchestrator, implementing none of the above",
   "originalText": "VariantAssigner   -> HashBucketAssigner\n     assign(experimentId, userId, experimentDef) -> variantKey\nExposureLogger    -> AsyncExposureLogger\n     logExposure(experimentId, userId, variantKey, timestamp)   # fire-and-forget\nMetricAggregator  -> WelfordMetricAggregator\n     ingest(experimentId, variantKey, metricName, value)\nSignificanceTest  -> TwoProportionZTest | WelchTTest\n     evaluate(controlSummary, treatmentSummary) -> {pValue, confidenceInterval}\nSrmChecker        -> ChiSquareSrmChecker\n     check(observedCounts, expectedAllocation) -> {chiSquareStat, pValue, flagged}\nExperimentAnalyzer  - the orchestrator, implementing none of the above",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "ifc",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1050,
   "y": 146,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100007,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700049,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A binary metric (did the user convert) uses the z-test for proportions; a\ncontinuous one (revenue per user) uses Welch's t-test, which does NOT assume the\ntwo variants have equal variance. Both sit behind one interface, so the analyzer\nnever knows which is running - and a future sequential test drops in without\ntouching it.",
   "originalText": "A binary metric (did the user convert) uses the z-test for proportions; a\ncontinuous one (revenue per user) uses Welch's t-test, which does NOT assume the\ntwo variants have equal variance. Both sit behind one interface, so the analyzer\nnever knows which is running - and a future sequential test drops in without\ntouching it.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1050,
   "y": 240,
   "width": 614,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100008,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700056,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The analyzer depends on all of them plus a PeekingGate, and implements none of the\nstorage, hashing or statistics itself. Which is what makes the extension\nquestions answerable: the interfaces already say which component should own each\nnew piece of behaviour, before you have worked out what the behaviour does.",
   "originalText": "The analyzer depends on all of them plus a PeekingGate, and implements none of the\nstorage, hashing or statistics itself. Which is what makes the extension\nquestions answerable: the interfaces already say which component should own each\nnew piece of behaviour, before you have worked out what the behaviour does.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d2",
