  {
   "id": "cn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 950,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100028,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700196,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "One user's exposure and conversion always land on the SAME partition, because the stream is sharded by user_id. Each partition\nmaintains its own triple with NO VISIBILITY INTO ANY OTHER PARTITION'S STATE AT ALL - and never retains a raw value, which is\nwhat makes a per-variant mean and variance computable without storing every observation.",
   "originalText": "One user's exposure and conversion always land on the SAME partition, because the stream is sharded by user_id. Each partition\nmaintains its own triple with NO VISIBILITY INTO ANY OTHER PARTITION'S STATE AT ALL - and never retains a raw value, which is\nwhat makes a per-variant mean and variance computable without storing every observation.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1400,
   "y": 646,
   "width": 182,
   "height": 345,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100029,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700203,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The merge step is the\nentire reason that is\nsafe: a PURE,\nASSOCIATIVE combination\nof two triples into one.\nIt does not matter which\norder partitions merge\nin, or how many merge at\nonce - the result is the\nsame either way.\n\nSo 'no coordination\nneeded' does not rest on\na lock that is fast\nenough. There is nothing\nto protect, because\nthere is no shared\nmutable state between\npartitions in the first\nplace - only independent\nlocal state and a pure\ncombining function\napplied afterward.",
   "originalText": "The merge step is the\nentire reason that is\nsafe: a PURE,\nASSOCIATIVE combination\nof two triples into one.\nIt does not matter which\norder partitions merge\nin, or how many merge at\nonce - the result is the\nsame either way.\n\nSo 'no coordination\nneeded' does not rest on\na lock that is fast\nenough. There is nothing\nto protect, because\nthere is no shared\nmutable state between\npartitions in the first\nplace - only independent\nlocal state and a pure\ncombining function\napplied afterward.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
