  {
   "id": "gate_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 1087,
   "width": 964,
   "height": 195,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100033,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700231,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "ExperimentAnalyzer.analyze(experimentId):\n    summaries = metricAggregator.currentSummaries(experimentId)\n\n    if not peekingGate.committedHorizonReached(experimentId, summaries):\n        return { status: 'monitoring_only',\n                 note: 'not a final read; do not act on this' }\n\n    srm = srmChecker.check(summaries.observedCounts, def.expectedAllocation)\n    if srm.flagged:\n        return { status: 'untrustworthy', reason: 'sample ratio mismatch' }\n\n    r = significanceTest.evaluate(summaries.control, summaries.treatment)\n    return { status: 'final', pValue: r.pValue, confidenceInterval: r.ci }",
   "originalText": "ExperimentAnalyzer.analyze(experimentId):\n    summaries = metricAggregator.currentSummaries(experimentId)\n\n    if not peekingGate.committedHorizonReached(experimentId, summaries):\n        return { status: 'monitoring_only',\n                 note: 'not a final read; do not act on this' }\n\n    srm = srmChecker.check(summaries.observedCounts, def.expectedAllocation)\n    if srm.flagged:\n        return { status: 'untrustworthy', reason: 'sample ratio mismatch' }\n\n    r = significanceTest.evaluate(summaries.control, summaries.treatment)\n    return { status: 'final', pValue: r.pValue, confidenceInterval: r.ci }",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "gate",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1050,
   "y": 1090,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100034,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700238,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "analyze() can be called as often as anyone likes - a dashboard hitting it once a\nminute causes no statistical harm - because the function itself REFUSES to hand\nback a 'final' verdict until the pre-registered sample size or duration has\nactually been hit.",
   "originalText": "analyze() can be called as often as anyone likes - a dashboard hitting it once a\nminute causes no statistical harm - because the function itself REFUSES to hand\nback a 'final' verdict until the pre-registered sample size or duration has\nactually been hit.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1050,
   "y": 1170,
   "width": 591,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100035,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700245,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Everything before that point is explicitly labelled 'monitoring_only': visible\nfor trend-watching, and STRUCTURALLY INCAPABLE of being read as 'significant,\nship it'. That is the peeking discipline enforced in code rather than left as a\npolicy somebody has to remember.",
   "originalText": "Everything before that point is explicitly labelled 'monitoring_only': visible\nfor trend-watching, and STRUCTURALLY INCAPABLE of being read as 'significant,\nship it'. That is the peeking discipline enforced in code rather than left as a\npolicy somebody has to remember.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1050,
   "y": 1250,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100036,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700252,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And note the ordering: SRM is checked BEFORE the significance test, and a flagged\nSRM returns 'untrustworthy' INSTEAD OF a p-value - not alongside one. A skewed\nsplit means control and treatment likely differ in ways beyond the treatment\nitself, so reporting a p-value over a broken comparison is worse than reporting\nnothing.",
   "originalText": "And note the ordering: SRM is checked BEFORE the significance test, and a flagged\nSRM returns 'untrustworthy' INSTEAD OF a p-value - not alongside one. A skewed\nsplit means control and treatment likely differ in ways beyond the treatment\nitself, so reporting a p-value over a broken comparison is worse than reporting\nnothing.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
