   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "read n     at t0    -> 4,812\nread mean  at t1    -> computed over 4,813 observations\n  -> the gate opens on a MIX of two different sample sizes",
   "originalText": "read n     at t0    -> 4,812\nread mean  at t1    -> computed over 4,813 observations\n  -> the gate opens on a MIX of two different sample sizes",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "bad",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 850,
   "y": 1716,
   "width": 591,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100052,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700364,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "committedHorizonReached() has to read a CONSISTENT SNAPSHOT of (n, mean,\nvariance). Reading n from one moment and mean from a slightly later one - after\nanother event has already been ingested - could let the gate open on a mixture\nthat never existed as a single state.",
   "originalText": "committedHorizonReached() has to read a CONSISTENT SNAPSHOT of (n, mean,\nvariance). Reading n from one moment and mean from a slightly later one - after\nanother event has already been ingested - could let the gate open on a mixture\nthat never existed as a single state.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "good",
