   "versionNonce": 700378,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "the aggregator publishes each triple as ONE atomic reference swap",
   "originalText": "the aggregator publishes each triple as ONE atomic reference swap",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "good",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 850,
   "y": 1816,
   "width": 584,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100055,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700385,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "So any reader - including the gate - always sees one fully-consistent triple,\nnever a partially-updated one. The same immutable-snapshot technique the\nfeature-flag design uses for its config swap: never mutate what a reader might\nalready be holding; publish a new whole object instead.",
   "originalText": "So any reader - including the gate - always sees one fully-consistent triple,\nnever a partially-updated one. The same immutable-snapshot technique the\nfeature-flag design uses for its config swap: never mutate what a reader might\nalready be holding; publish a new whole object instead.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
